# Rank 1434 / CVE-2019-20445 (netty 8494b046ec): HttpObjectDecoder.readHeaders
# parsed the whole HTTP/1 header block and then chose the body framing from it
# with no reconciliation:
#
#   if (isContentAlwaysEmpty(message)) { ... }
#   else if (HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(message)) nextState = READ_CHUNK_SIZE;
#   else if (contentLength() >= 0)                        nextState = READ_FIXED_LENGTH_CONTENT;
#   else                                                  nextState = READ_VARIABLE_LENGTH_CONTENT;
#
# Two headers can each declare a body length, so a message that carries both --
# or that carries Content-Length twice with different values -- has two readings.
# The decoder took the first: chunked wins over Content-Length, and
# HttpUtil.getContentLength returns only the first of several Content-Length
# values. Nothing rejected the message. RFC 7230 requires the opposite in both
# cases: 3.3.2 says a recipient of duplicate Content-Length "MUST either reject
# the message as invalid or replace the duplicated field-values with a single
# valid Content-Length field", and 3.3.3 says a message carrying both
# Transfer-Encoding and Content-Length "might indicate an attempt to perform
# request smuggling ... and ought to be handled as an error", with a forwarder
# required to remove the Content-Length before passing it on.
#
# The weakness is not in netty's own bytes -- the decoder frames its stream
# self-consistently. It is in the disagreement with whatever else parses the
# same connection. A front-end proxy that resolves the ambiguity the other way
# and netty behind it draw the message boundary in different places, so the tail
# of one request becomes the head of the next: request smuggling, CWE-444. Fix
# 8494b046ec adds both checks to readHeaders -- headers.getAll(CONTENT_LENGTH)
# so the count can be compared, and an IllegalArgumentException for either
# conflict when the version is HTTP/1.1.
#
# FIXED. There is nothing tainted to follow: the attacker's input *is* the
# header block this method is parsing, so the weakness is a property of the
# parser and not of a value reaching a sink. code.AmbiguousMessageBodyFraming
# and rule VYQL-INJ-249 (CWE-444) judge it, and the Java binding names the
# method by what the reconciliation needs to be in one place: it accumulates
# parsed header lines into the message's header store, it asks whether the
# transfer encoding is chunked, and it asks for the content length. All three
# are required. netty's own encoder consults isTransferEncodingChunked without
# ever building a header store, and HttpServerKeepAliveHandler reads
# isContentLengthSet and isTransferEncodingChunked together for a keep-alive
# decision rather than a framing one; neither is reported, and both are pinned
# below.
#
# The negation lists the remedies RFC 7230 itself names, in the spellings a Java
# decoder uses: refusing the message (IllegalArgumentException, DecoderException,
# TooLongFrameException, invalidMessage, a failed DecoderResult) and dropping the
# duplicate (headers.remove of the Content-Length, or getAll/getAllAsString so
# every value is in hand). It deliberately does not look for a particular
# comparison -- a parser that rejects, or that normalises the header away, has
# discharged the obligation however it spells the test -- which is also what
# keeps the binding off the fixing commit's own layout: the two reject cases
# below discharge it with DecoderException and with headers.remove, neither of
# which appears in netty's patch, and both are silent.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off), identical across
# three runs. netty codec-http + codec-http2, 503 java files including tests, at
# 8494b046ec^: 33 findings, exactly one VYQL-INJ-249, at
# codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectDecoder.java:568,
# the CVE method; at 8494b046ec: 32 findings and no VYQL-INJ-249, no other
# finding moving. The whole netty tree at 8494b046ec^ -- every codec module,
# memcache, mqtt, redis, stomp, haproxy, socks and dns among them -- reports the
# same single row. logging-log4j2 (2237 java) reports none. No identifier this
# binding names appears anywhere in the OWASP Java Benchmark corpus, which
# contains no headers.add or headers.set call at all.

test "rank1434: an HTTP/1 header-block parser that frames the body from Transfer-Encoding or Content-Length without reconciling them"
  lang java
  file codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectDecoder.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-249
  expect_review code.AmbiguousMessageBodyFraming
  code
  ```
  package io.netty.handler.codec.http;

  import io.netty.buffer.ByteBuf;

  public abstract class HttpObjectDecoder {

      private State readHeaders(ByteBuf buffer) {
          final HttpMessage message = this.message;
          final HttpHeaders headers = message.headers();

          AppendableCharSequence line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
          if (line == null) {
              return null;
          }
          if (line.length() > 0) {
              do {
                  char firstChar = line.charAtUnsafe(0);
                  if (name != null && (firstChar == ' ' || firstChar == '\t')) {
                      String trimmedLine = line.toString().trim();
                      String valueStr = String.valueOf(value);
                      value = valueStr + ' ' + trimmedLine;
                  } else {
                      if (name != null) {
                          headers.add(name, value);
                      }
                      splitHeader(line);
                  }

                  line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
                  if (line == null) {
                      return null;
                  }
              } while (line.length() > 0);
          }

          if (name != null) {
              headers.add(name, value);
          }
          name = null;
          value = null;

          State nextState;

          if (isContentAlwaysEmpty(message)) {
              HttpUtil.setTransferEncodingChunked(message, false);
              nextState = State.SKIP_CONTROL_CHARS;
          } else if (HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(message)) {
              nextState = State.READ_CHUNK_SIZE;
          } else if (contentLength() >= 0) {
              nextState = State.READ_FIXED_LENGTH_CONTENT;
          } else {
              nextState = State.READ_VARIABLE_LENGTH_CONTENT;
          }
          return nextState;
      }

      private long contentLength() {
          if (contentLength == Long.MIN_VALUE) {
              contentLength = HttpUtil.getContentLength(message, -1L);
          }
          return contentLength;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1434: the fixed revision counts every Content-Length value and refuses a message that also declares chunked framing"
  lang java
  file codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectDecoder.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-249
  code
  ```
  package io.netty.handler.codec.http;

  import io.netty.buffer.ByteBuf;
  import java.util.List;

  public abstract class HttpObjectDecoder {

      private State readHeaders(ByteBuf buffer) {
          final HttpMessage message = this.message;
          final HttpHeaders headers = message.headers();

          AppendableCharSequence line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
          if (line == null) {
              return null;
          }
          if (line.length() > 0) {
              do {
                  char firstChar = line.charAtUnsafe(0);
                  if (name != null && (firstChar == ' ' || firstChar == '\t')) {
                      String trimmedLine = line.toString().trim();
                      String valueStr = String.valueOf(value);
                      value = valueStr + ' ' + trimmedLine;
                  } else {
                      if (name != null) {
                          headers.add(name, value);
                      }
                      splitHeader(line);
                  }

                  line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
                  if (line == null) {
                      return null;
                  }
              } while (line.length() > 0);
          }

          if (name != null) {
              headers.add(name, value);
          }
          name = null;
          value = null;

          List<String> values = headers.getAll(HttpHeaderNames.CONTENT_LENGTH);
          int contentLengthValuesCount = values.size();

          if (contentLengthValuesCount > 0) {
              if (contentLengthValuesCount > 1 && message.protocolVersion() == HttpVersion.HTTP_1_1) {
                  throw new IllegalArgumentException("Multiple Content-Length headers found");
              }
              contentLength = Long.parseLong(values.get(0));
          }

          if (isContentAlwaysEmpty(message)) {
              HttpUtil.setTransferEncodingChunked(message, false);
              return State.SKIP_CONTROL_CHARS;
          } else if (HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(message)) {
              if (contentLengthValuesCount > 0 && message.protocolVersion() == HttpVersion.HTTP_1_1) {
                  throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                          "Both 'Content-Length: " + contentLength + "' and 'Transfer-Encoding: chunked' found");
              }
              return State.READ_CHUNK_SIZE;
          } else if (contentLength() >= 0) {
              return State.READ_FIXED_LENGTH_CONTENT;
          } else {
              return State.READ_VARIABLE_LENGTH_CONTENT;
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1434: a parser that refuses the ambiguous message with a decoder exception instead is not reported"
  lang java
  file codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/StrictHttpMessageDecoder.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-249
  code
  ```
  package io.netty.handler.codec.http;

  import io.netty.buffer.ByteBuf;
  import io.netty.handler.codec.DecoderException;

  public abstract class StrictHttpMessageDecoder {

      private State readHeaders(ByteBuf buffer) {
          final HttpMessage message = this.message;
          final HttpHeaders headers = message.headers();

          AppendableCharSequence line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
          while (line != null && line.length() > 0) {
              splitHeader(line);
              headers.add(name, value);
              line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
          }

          if (HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(message) && contentLength() >= 0) {
              throw new DecoderException("Transfer-Encoding and Content-Length both present");
          }

          if (HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(message)) {
              return State.READ_CHUNK_SIZE;
          } else if (contentLength() >= 0) {
              return State.READ_FIXED_LENGTH_CONTENT;
          }
          return State.READ_VARIABLE_LENGTH_CONTENT;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1434: a parser that drops the Content-Length header when a transfer encoding is present is not reported"
  lang java
  file codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/NormalizingHttpMessageDecoder.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-249
  code
  ```
  package io.netty.handler.codec.http;

  import io.netty.buffer.ByteBuf;

  public abstract class NormalizingHttpMessageDecoder {

      private State readHeaders(ByteBuf buffer) {
          final HttpMessage message = this.message;
          final HttpHeaders headers = message.headers();

          AppendableCharSequence line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
          while (line != null && line.length() > 0) {
              splitHeader(line);
              headers.add(name, value);
              line = headerParser.parse(buffer);
          }

          if (HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(message)) {
              headers.remove(HttpHeaderNames.CONTENT_LENGTH);
              return State.READ_CHUNK_SIZE;
          } else if (contentLength() >= 0) {
              return State.READ_FIXED_LENGTH_CONTENT;
          }
          return State.READ_VARIABLE_LENGTH_CONTENT;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1434: an encoder that picks a chunked write path without ever parsing a header block is not reported"
  lang java
  file codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectEncoder.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-249
  code
  ```
  package io.netty.handler.codec.http;

  import io.netty.buffer.ByteBuf;

  public abstract class HttpObjectEncoder {

      protected void encode(Object msg, ByteBuf buf) {
          HttpMessage m = (HttpMessage) msg;
          state = HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(m) ? ST_CONTENT_CHUNK : ST_CONTENT_NON_CHUNK;
          encodeInitialLine(buf, m);
          encodeHeaders(m.headers(), buf);
          long length = contentLength();
          buf.writeShort(CRLF_SHORT);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1434: a keep-alive policy helper that reads both framing headers without parsing a header block is not reported"
  lang java
  file codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpServerKeepAliveHandler.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-249
  code
  ```
  package io.netty.handler.codec.http;

  public class HttpServerKeepAliveHandler {

      private static boolean shouldSelfClose(HttpResponse response) {
          return HttpUtil.isContentLengthSet(response) || HttpUtil.isTransferEncodingChunked(response)
                  || contentLength() >= 0;
      }
  }
  ```
